# purpose: CI's `policy` check on every pull request: the branch kind decides what it may change (`wsc policy`, docs/CONSUMING.md "The job pipeline");
#          a failure comments on the pull request.
# usage: runs on GitHub Actions; locally: python3 wsc.py policy --branch <branch> --base origin/main
# when: automatic on pull requests; require the "policy" check in branch protection for main.
# Draft pull requests skip it: a job's builder opens its pull request as a draft when the job reaches review, so the review sees the branch's CI
# without a `policy` that must fail until the review says merge. The reviewer marks the pull request ready BEFORE pushing the review commit
# (a skipped policy counts as passed, and `gh pr merge --auto` merges at once when the checks have passed), so the pushed head gets a real
# `policy` run; the ready_for_review run on the old head has no merge verdict and is red by design: the push cancels it, and `notify` stays silent.
name: policy
on:
  pull_request:
    types: [opened, synchronize, reopened, ready_for_review]
permissions:
  contents: read
concurrency:
  group: policy-${{ github.event.pull_request.number }}
  cancel-in-progress: true
jobs:
{{wsc policy}}
{{wsc notify policy}}
